    model: "Failure was traditionally defined as premature return, but the high rates come from old, poorly sourced studies (Harzing called them a myth) and must be interpreted with caution. The definition is too narrow: underperformance and quitting after repatriation are also failures, and some early returns are successes. Individual and organizational views differ, so include subjective indicators like career and life satisfaction. The debate still helped by drawing attention to selection, training, family support and repatriation.",
